1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:03,990
Here's something that has bothered
me for a surprisingly long time.

2
00:00:04,320 --> 00:00:07,150
A radio signal leaves an antenna on Earth.

3
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:11,590
It crosses more than half a billion
kilometres of absolutely nothing.

4
00:00:12,340 --> 00:00:15,230
And then it arrives at a
spacecraft near Jupiter.

5
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:18,510
Vanishingly faint, spread impossibly thin.

6
00:00:18,940 --> 00:00:20,770
But still the same signal.

7
00:00:21,613 --> 00:00:26,383
Every wave I can actually picture needs
something to wave. Sound needs air.

8
00:00:26,673 --> 00:00:30,383
Ripples need water. A wave
on a rope needs the rope.

9
00:00:31,226 --> 00:00:34,316
So if a radio signal travels
through empty space...

10
00:00:34,526 --> 00:00:36,756
what exactly is the wave waving?

11
00:00:37,530 --> 00:00:41,130
For most of the nineteenth century,
physicists had an answer they were quite

12
00:00:41,210 --> 00:00:44,500
happy with. Space
couldn't really be empty.

13
00:00:45,010 --> 00:00:46,920
It had to be filled with something.

14
00:00:47,370 --> 00:00:50,480
An invisible substance that
light could ripple through.

15
00:00:50,870 --> 00:00:52,980
They called it the luminiferous ether.

16
00:00:53,975 --> 00:00:58,325
And then, in eighteen eighty-seven, two
men in Cleveland went looking for it.

17
00:00:58,595 --> 00:01:00,045
They didn't find it.

18
00:01:00,900 --> 00:01:02,650
So the ether was in trouble.

19
00:01:03,240 --> 00:01:04,640
But the problem wasn't.

20
00:01:04,720 --> 00:01:07,090
If waves need something to wave...

21
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:09,850
what exactly was moving
through empty space?

22
00:01:10,280 --> 00:01:14,290
To understand how physicists got
there, we need to go back a little.

23
00:01:15,039 --> 00:01:19,239
In the early nineteenth century,
electricity and magnetism looked like two

24
00:01:19,319 --> 00:01:20,909
completely different things.

25
00:01:21,359 --> 00:01:22,899
Then something strange happened.

26
00:01:22,979 --> 00:01:28,319
Hans Christian Ørsted discovered that an
electric current could affect a compass

27
00:01:28,399 --> 00:01:32,029
needle. Electricity and
magnetism were connected.

28
00:01:33,019 --> 00:01:37,179
And André-Marie Ampère quickly developed
a mathematical description of that

29
00:01:37,259 --> 00:01:42,529
connection. A current flowing through a
wire creates a magnetic field around it.

30
00:01:42,839 --> 00:01:45,369
Electricity could create magnetism.

31
00:01:46,153 --> 00:01:47,883
Then came another surprise.

32
00:01:48,813 --> 00:01:51,663
Michael Faraday discovered
electromagnetic induction.

33
00:01:52,293 --> 00:01:55,723
A changing magnetic field could
produce an electric current.

34
00:01:56,333 --> 00:01:58,723
Now the connection worked
in the other direction too.

35
00:01:59,930 --> 00:02:01,840
But there was an important detail.

36
00:02:02,510 --> 00:02:06,140
A steady electric current
produces a steady magnetic field.

37
00:02:06,710 --> 00:02:08,280
And once nothing is changing...

38
00:02:08,750 --> 00:02:11,420
there is nothing new to
propagate outward as a wave.

39
00:02:12,070 --> 00:02:13,900
For radiation, change matters.

40
00:02:14,944 --> 00:02:16,674
Then there was another problem.

41
00:02:16,784 --> 00:02:19,194
Imagine charging a capacitor.

42
00:02:20,284 --> 00:02:21,684
Electric current flows
through the wires...

43
00:02:21,764 --> 00:02:24,754
and charge builds up on two metal plates.

44
00:02:25,647 --> 00:02:28,017
But between the plates... there is a gap.

45
00:02:28,587 --> 00:02:31,317
No ordinary electric current crosses it.

46
00:02:31,687 --> 00:02:35,827
And yet the changing electric field
still had to play a role. Otherwise...

47
00:02:35,907 --> 00:02:38,857
the picture didn't add
up. Something was missing.

48
00:02:39,786 --> 00:02:42,556
Then James Clerk Maxwell
took the next step.

49
00:02:42,986 --> 00:02:46,756
He proposed that a changing electric
field could have a magnetic effect...

50
00:02:47,286 --> 00:02:50,256
even where no ordinary
electric current was flowing.

51
00:02:50,726 --> 00:02:53,216
This was the idea of displacement current.

52
00:02:54,137 --> 00:02:56,667
Now the two sides finally fit together.

53
00:02:57,077 --> 00:03:00,887
Changing electric and magnetic
fields were not separate phenomena.

54
00:03:01,417 --> 00:03:04,007
They were part of one
electromagnetic system.

55
00:03:04,839 --> 00:03:07,369
And that system allowed
something extraordinary.

56
00:03:08,119 --> 00:03:13,009
A disturbance could propagate through
space. Not through water. Not through air.

57
00:03:13,399 --> 00:03:16,049
But as a changing electromagnetic field.

58
00:03:16,865 --> 00:03:20,345
It is tempting to imagine this as
one field creating the other...

59
00:03:20,425 --> 00:03:23,875
then the other creating the
first... over and over again.

60
00:03:24,285 --> 00:03:25,695
That picture is useful.

61
00:03:26,425 --> 00:03:28,675
But reality is a little subtler.

62
00:03:29,085 --> 00:03:33,735
The electric and magnetic fields are
parts of the same electromagnetic wave.

63
00:03:34,588 --> 00:03:38,668
Maxwell's equations predicted that these
disturbances should travel at a very

64
00:03:38,748 --> 00:03:42,078
specific speed. So he calculated it.

65
00:03:42,468 --> 00:03:46,578
The answer was approximately three
hundred thousand kilometres per second.

66
00:03:47,381 --> 00:03:49,191
Does that number seem familiar?

67
00:03:50,123 --> 00:03:51,733
It was the speed of light.

68
00:03:52,693 --> 00:03:56,423
And that was one of the great surprises
of nineteenth-century physics.

69
00:03:56,993 --> 00:04:00,083
Light itself appeared to
be an electromagnetic wave.

70
00:04:00,919 --> 00:04:03,889
But a prediction is not the
same thing as an experiment.

71
00:04:04,479 --> 00:04:07,569
Someone had to show that
these waves actually existed.

72
00:04:08,484 --> 00:04:12,114
In the eighteen eighties,
Heinrich Hertz did exactly that.

73
00:04:12,324 --> 00:04:16,354
He generated electromagnetic
waves. And detected them.

74
00:04:17,094 --> 00:04:22,094
Maxwell's strange mathematical
prediction was real. And yes. That Hertz.

75
00:04:22,354 --> 00:04:26,644
The same unit you see when someone tells
you the frequency of a radio signal.

76
00:04:27,411 --> 00:04:31,761
At almost exactly the same time,
physics was discovering something else.

77
00:04:32,231 --> 00:04:33,621
The waves were real.

78
00:04:33,731 --> 00:04:36,231
But the medium they were
supposed to travel through...

79
00:04:36,311 --> 00:04:37,961
could not be found.

80
00:04:38,817 --> 00:04:42,717
In eighteen eighty-seven, Albert Michelson
and Edward Morley were looking for

81
00:04:42,797 --> 00:04:45,547
evidence of that medium. The ether.

82
00:04:46,423 --> 00:04:49,893
But Maxwell himself did not think
this meant the ether was gone.

83
00:04:50,283 --> 00:04:55,903
He believed his electromagnetic theory was
describing phenomena that still existed in

84
00:04:55,983 --> 00:04:59,453
a physical medium. The
ether was not dead yet.

85
00:05:00,325 --> 00:05:04,785
It took decades, and a major change in
the way physicists thought about space and

86
00:05:04,865 --> 00:05:08,475
time, before the idea of an
ether became unnecessary.

87
00:05:09,185 --> 00:05:13,635
The wave no longer needed an invisible
mechanical substance to travel through.

88
00:05:14,354 --> 00:05:16,624
And something else was becoming clear.

89
00:05:17,014 --> 00:05:21,414
For thousands of years, there had been one
kind of electromagnetic radiation humans

90
00:05:21,494 --> 00:05:23,904
knew very well. Light.

91
00:05:24,820 --> 00:05:30,080
Then the spectrum started expanding.
Infrared. Ultraviolet. And eventually...

92
00:05:30,160 --> 00:05:31,570
radio waves.

93
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:34,890
At first, they looked like
completely different phenomena.

94
00:05:35,821 --> 00:05:38,021
Radio waves. Microwaves. Infrared.

95
00:05:38,101 --> 00:05:41,971
Visible light. Ultraviolet.
X-rays. Gamma rays.

96
00:05:42,808 --> 00:05:44,838
They are not seven different things.

97
00:05:45,288 --> 00:05:48,798
Maxwell's theory, and Hertz's
experiments, revealed the connection.

98
00:05:49,368 --> 00:05:51,598
They are all electromagnetic radiation.

99
00:05:52,700 --> 00:05:55,190
They differ mainly in
frequency and wavelength.

100
00:05:56,020 --> 00:06:00,270
And those differences give them very
different properties. But underneath...

101
00:06:00,500 --> 00:06:03,150
they belong to the same
electromagnetic family.

102
00:06:04,043 --> 00:06:06,173
So when your radio receives a signal...

103
00:06:06,463 --> 00:06:08,633
when your phone talks to a Wi-Fi router...

104
00:06:09,003 --> 00:06:10,873
when Bluetooth connects your headphones...

105
00:06:11,403 --> 00:06:13,773
or when light from the
Sun reaches your eyes...

106
00:06:14,143 --> 00:06:17,773
you are dealing with different parts
of the same electromagnetic spectrum.

107
00:06:18,496 --> 00:06:21,426
And humans became
extremely good at using it.

108
00:06:21,756 --> 00:06:25,726
We build antennas that deliberately
launch electromagnetic waves.

109
00:06:26,296 --> 00:06:28,146
Other antennas detect them.

110
00:06:28,921 --> 00:06:31,691
Which raises a slightly
ridiculous question.

111
00:06:32,141 --> 00:06:36,391
If radio waves and visible light are
both electromagnetic radiation...

112
00:06:37,121 --> 00:06:39,531
could you build an antenna
that transmits light?

113
00:06:40,369 --> 00:06:43,199
Actually... the antenna
is not the difficult part.

114
00:06:43,789 --> 00:06:47,669
For green light, a simple half-wave dipole
would be only a few hundred nanometres

115
00:06:47,749 --> 00:06:49,959
long. That is tiny.

116
00:06:50,629 --> 00:06:52,299
But not impossible to manufacture.

117
00:06:53,610 --> 00:06:56,160
The real problem is making it oscillate.

118
00:06:56,530 --> 00:07:00,980
Visible light has a frequency of hundreds
of trillions of cycles per second.

119
00:07:01,470 --> 00:07:03,360
We can build a nanoscale antenna.

120
00:07:04,170 --> 00:07:08,140
But driving it with ordinary
electronics is another matter entirely.

121
00:07:09,008 --> 00:07:12,018
And now we can return to
that signal leaving Earth.

122
00:07:12,468 --> 00:07:17,198
As an electromagnetic wave travels
farther from its source... it spreads out.

123
00:07:18,023 --> 00:07:22,293
Imagine the energy from the transmitter
expanding outward through space.

124
00:07:22,763 --> 00:07:27,053
A little farther away, the same
energy is spread over a larger area.

125
00:07:27,483 --> 00:07:30,113
And farther still...
over a much larger one.

126
00:07:30,881 --> 00:07:33,371
Nothing is necessarily "wearing out".

127
00:07:33,921 --> 00:07:35,531
The wave is simply spreading.

128
00:07:36,221 --> 00:07:37,831
The farther you get from the source...

129
00:07:38,341 --> 00:07:41,271
the less of that energy
reaches any particular area.

130
00:07:42,053 --> 00:07:45,583
For an ideal source radiating
equally in all directions...

131
00:07:46,293 --> 00:07:50,163
the available power per square metre
falls with the square of the distance.

132
00:07:50,733 --> 00:07:54,853
Twice as far away... only a quarter
as much. Ten times farther...

133
00:07:54,933 --> 00:07:56,903
one hundred times less.

134
00:07:57,769 --> 00:08:00,779
And yet... with the right
transmitter... the right antenna...

135
00:08:01,349 --> 00:08:02,979
and a sensitive enough receiver...

136
00:08:03,549 --> 00:08:07,299
even an incredibly tiny fraction of
that signal can still be detected.

137
00:08:08,211 --> 00:08:11,101
That is how we can send
signals across the planet.

138
00:08:11,571 --> 00:08:13,261
Across the Solar System.

139
00:08:13,831 --> 00:08:18,741
And turn tiny disturbances in an
electromagnetic field into sound. Images.

140
00:08:19,551 --> 00:08:20,761
Data. Messages.

141
00:08:21,730 --> 00:08:24,140
And now look at what we
can do with all of this.

142
00:08:24,630 --> 00:08:28,560
We can describe electromagnetic
fields with extraordinary precision.

143
00:08:29,150 --> 00:08:33,640
We can predict how they behave. We
use them to see. To communicate.

144
00:08:34,590 --> 00:08:36,040
To understand the universe.

145
00:08:37,023 --> 00:08:38,773
But if you keep asking why...

146
00:08:38,863 --> 00:08:40,973
the original question comes back.

147
00:08:41,483 --> 00:08:43,073
A water wave has water.

148
00:08:43,843 --> 00:08:45,353
A sound wave has air.

149
00:08:45,983 --> 00:08:47,793
A wave on a rope has a rope.

150
00:08:48,688 --> 00:08:50,268
An electromagnetic wave has...

151
00:08:50,348 --> 00:08:52,518
the electromagnetic field.

152
00:08:53,328 --> 00:08:54,758
That is the answer.

153
00:08:55,308 --> 00:08:57,398
But it may not feel like an answer.

154
00:08:57,828 --> 00:09:01,038
Because now we have simply
replaced one question with another.

155
00:09:01,748 --> 00:09:03,518
What exactly is a field?

156
00:09:04,048 --> 00:09:05,558
Is it a physical thing?

157
00:09:06,068 --> 00:09:10,698
Or just a mathematical way of describing
what happens at every point in space?

158
00:09:11,619 --> 00:09:13,509
Modern physics goes further.

159
00:09:14,019 --> 00:09:17,949
In quantum field theory, the
electromagnetic field is fundamental.

160
00:09:18,639 --> 00:09:21,629
What we call a photon is an
excitation of that field.

161
00:09:22,259 --> 00:09:24,949
And this description works
extraordinarily well.

162
00:09:25,694 --> 00:09:28,464
But describing something with
extraordinary precision...

163
00:09:28,834 --> 00:09:31,134
and answering what it ultimately is...

164
00:09:31,214 --> 00:09:33,384
are not necessarily the same question.

165
00:09:34,595 --> 00:09:37,105
Maybe that is the part
I find most fascinating.

166
00:09:37,795 --> 00:09:39,115
We stopped looking for the ether.

167
00:09:39,195 --> 00:09:44,075
And learned how to describe
electromagnetic fields so well that we

168
00:09:44,155 --> 00:09:46,225
built the modern world on top of them.

169
00:09:46,861 --> 00:09:48,731
But the deeper you push the question...

170
00:09:49,001 --> 00:09:53,271
the less it sounds like something from a
physics textbook. What is actually waving?

171
00:09:54,767 --> 00:09:57,357
The answer is: the electromagnetic field.

172
00:09:57,847 --> 00:10:00,857
And then, almost immediately,
comes the next question.

173
00:10:01,207 --> 00:10:02,817
What exactly is a field?
